✔ the warden reacts only after its reaction delay: no defensive input can answer an attack it has not yet noticed (44.497334ms)
✔ an unblockable swing it cannot parry or roll is answered with a backstep out of reach (1.680291ms)
✔ the warden uses the same combat API: its attacks cost stamina, obey range and resolve through the same contact rules (63.676833ms)
✔ a passive opponent sees a readable opener: at easy and normal the first attack is always a heavy, later ones heavy or thrust; hard also pressures with lights (451.651208ms)
✔ against a settled guard the warden holds its heavy to the charge that breaks it, and releases as soon as it is charged (45.174709ms)
✔ the warden punishes a whiff with a light and kicks or breaks a standing guard (102.414875ms)
✔ parry frequency follows the profile: a light-spamming player is parried at hard and never by a profile without parries (306.409125ms)
✔ the warden never idles out of reach: a stationary guarding fighter is attacked at least every eight seconds at every level (175.232875ms)
✔ the warden moves with seeded, bounded decisions, stays in the arena and waits for the player to draw (67.082375ms)
✔ the warden reads only committed state: identical duels decide identically, and pending player input changes nothing (2.755209ms)
✔ difficulty changes outcomes through reaction, defence and aggression, not through different rules (277.835792ms)
✔ a landed blow earns a punish window: the warden never counter-attacks the instant its stagger ends (2.2685ms)
✔ posture: a shaky warden gives ground so its bar drains, and finishes a broken player with the critical rather than a riposte (1.32875ms)
✔ reads: habits become reads only with evidence, at the documented thresholds (9.713542ms)
✔ the warden adapts: a turtle is kicked and charged through more; a light-spammer is parried more; a roller sees delayed swings and tail punishes; a parrier gets baited lights (392.002125ms)
✔ the thrust: a minority opener planned only after the first heavy, thrown from wherever it stands (no walk-back), never into a guard — and the stop-hit into an opponent walking onto the point (200.210916ms)
✔ perception runs on elapsed time: a heavy parked at its chamber is noticed and answered on the normal reaction clock (0.709958ms)
✔ fairness pass: the warden uses its own tools against pressure — the guard counter after a block, the punish of a whiffed parry, a guard walk (never a slow opener, never a standing wait) into a read spammer, and feints at a parrier (16.217292ms)
✔ a kick is never guarded or parried: with its dodge share the warden rolls it (steps out without the stamina), otherwise it takes the poke (64.025416ms)
✔ habits are counted from what the player actually threw: a thrust is a thrust, not a cut — and no profile reacts faster than a human can (9.003042ms)
✔ the ring wall in the warden's footwork: a retreat that would put its back to the wall becomes a circle inward, and a player pinned on the wall is pressed straight (0.427834ms)
✔ attrition and the stamina floor: a warden whose ceiling has been cut below its discipline floor still fights (the floor is a share of the ceiling), never circles for ever (0.163209ms)
✔ feint knob: a feinting fighter feints anyone (the read-parrier's sixth still applies on top); without the knob a passive player is never feinted (61.111458ms)
✔ guard knob 0: the fighter never stands in guard, never baits with one, never blocks and never guard-walks — it evades or steps back instead; the same seeds with the default guard do all of those (404.810333ms)
✔ disengage knob: after a landed blow the fighter hops back out of range on most of them; without the knob it never steps back after landing (172.255625ms)
✔ circle knob: a circler drifts sideways while closing in; the default walks straight (0.838083ms)
✔ regen knob: a fighter built with regen 2 refills stamina twice as fast; the default is RULES.regen (0.627333ms)
✔ step knob: a kick that a backstep will clear is stepped out of (10 stamina), not rolled (30); a blow the step cannot clear is still rolled; without the knob the roll is the dodge (8.903959ms)
✔ interrupt knob: a fast fighter cuts INTO a slow tell that his cut beats; without the knob no one attacks into a threat (0.361084ms)
✔ kick knob: against a read roller or backstepper a kicker kicks (the one blow their timing does not escape); the default only kicks a guard (104.844625ms)
✔ dash knob: a darter sprints into an opening from outside reach; the default walks (0.511834ms)
✔ pace: an opponent with speed 1.2 walks, lunges and steps 1.2× as far per tick; a man is unchanged (1.628333ms)
✔ one step out, then walking: an evade plan takes the backstep only while inside the blow's reach and walks back once out — never a chain of backsteps (0.701458ms)
✔ a chain follow-up the cut cannot reach goes as the thrust when the chain allows it (the goblin's slash → thrust); a sword cut, whose chain has no thrust, does not (2.19475ms)
✔ a fighter with no guard respects a read poker's or kicker's reach: he hovers at its edge instead of walking onto the point, and goes in on the whiff (0.665084ms)
